<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aden Abdullah Osman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1908–2007</span> · Also known as Aden Adde</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> Abdullah Osman, known as Aden Adde, was the first president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>. A leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somali-youth-league">Somali Youth League</a>, he became president when the Trust Territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> and the State of Somaliland united as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> Republic on 1 July 1960. He lost the 1967 election and handed over power peacefully, a rare example in post-colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aden-abdullah-osman.jpg" alt="Aden Abdullah Osman" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Somalia Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aden_Abdulle_Osman_Daar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
